{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>From among all the beasts that are upon the earth</b> – Its plain sense: from among all the beasts that are upon the face of the whole earth, like the sense of מִכָּל אֲשֶׁר בָּעוֹלָם (\"from all that is in the world\"). And its midrash (Torat Kohanim, Parashah 2): since there are beasts in the sea and their law is not determined by these signs but rather like fish, therefore it says \"that are upon the earth\" to exclude that which is in the sea."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:52:24.829472296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}